From 719995193cc6a419d1e0d41b9e42012fa75a58e3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 11:11:27 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Fix Sell page search dropping matches; search by product type
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Root cause: findMatches() sorted the matches and then cut the list to
MAX_SEARCH_RESULTS = 8. Ties were ordered alphabetically, so on "joint" the
Capablanco/Ceresit/Mapei products filled the 8 slots and the Sika products
were silently left out (while "sika" still found them). Every match is listed
now; ordering only decides what is seen first.

Search (shared by the Sell box and the Stock filter):
- normalizeSearchText(): lower case, accents removed, punctuation and extra
  spaces collapsed, 60*60 / 60x60 / 60 × 60 alike; any script is kept.
- AND matching: every typed word must be in name, manufacturer, tile size,
  SKU, category or product type.
- The existing productType value is searched through its words in every
  language (Pâte à joint / Faïence / Pierre / Rock / Arabic ...). No second
  type system; nothing stored is changed.
- A field an older product lacks no longer becomes the word "undefined".
- Ranking no longer splits words at the letter "x".

I18n.textIn(code, key) added (text of a key in one given language).
tests/sell-search.test.js added; the old "at most 8 results" test, which
pinned the bug in place, now asserts every match is listed.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
